{{also|Amma|ammā|ämmä}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæmə/}}
* {{rhymes|en|æmə}}

===Etymology 1===
Related to {{cog|syc|ܐܡܐ||tr=emma}}, {{cog|hi|अम्मा}}, {{cog|ml|അമ്മ|sc=Mlym}}, {{cog|kn|ಅಮ್ಮ||mother}} {{cog|te|అమ్మ||mother}}, {{cog|si|අම්මා||mother}}, or {{cog|ta|அம்மா||mother}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# [[mother]]

====Usage notes====
* Widely used in English-speaking [[expat]] communities.

====See also====
* {{l|en|amah}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor|en|LL.|amma}} {{lena}}, probably of interjectional or imitative origin: compare {{cog|es|ama}}, {{cog|de|Amme}}, {{cog|eu|ama}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# An [[abbess]] or [[spiritual]] [[mother]].

{{Webster 1913}}

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|a=aamm|ma ma|ma'am|mama}}

